d22963c:.claude/skills/bootstrap/templates/ARCHITECTURE.md:42:- **A client component reads data with TanStack Query's `useQuery`,** through a server action, and never with an effect or a check of its own for which answer is the newest (`factory/decisions.md` [S669a](factory/decisions/669.md)). The cache is `getQueryClient` in `src/lib/query`: a new one for each request on the server, so no answer crosses from one request to another, and one in the browser for as long as the page is open. `QueryProvider` in `src/lib/query/query-provider.tsx` gives it to every page from `src/app/layout.tsx`. A server component that has the data reads it ahead, inside `<Suspense>`, with `prefetchQuery` on its own `getQueryClient()`, and hands it to the browser in a `HydrationBoundary`, with the same `queryOptions` the client component reads with. A change still goes through a server action. The version under the waitlist is the example (see "Reference feature").
